# ============================================================================
# Mia — look to talk.
#
#   A communication board for someone who can't use their hands. Look around
#   the tiles; the one you rest on lights up; rest / open your mouth / blink and
#   Mia speaks it aloud. Touch works too, for a carer setting it up.
#
#   The head-tracking is the engine's — Mia only consumes the cursor+click
#   events (Face), so it needs no camera code of its own and drives no OS
#   pointer; it just lights its own tiles. Same head-mouse engine Andy uses.
#
#   Made with Visualised.  Part of the Mia assistive kit, Wallisoft.
# ============================================================================

@Window Mia
Title=Mia
Version=0.1.0
Width=484
Height=660
AppBar=true
Accent=#7C3AED
About=Mia — a look-to-talk communication board. Rest, open your mouth or blink to speak a tile. Made with Visualised.
